{"key": "eagle3", "name": "EAGLE-3", "date": "2025-03", "arxiv": "2503.01840", "skill": "fused multi-layer features; train on own drafts", "solves": [["EAGLE-2", "feature-regression loss caps gains from more data"], ["EAGLE-2", "trained on target features, drafts on its own (exposure bias)"]], "later_fixes": {"drafting is autoregressive too: k serial passes per draft": ["P-EAGLE", "DART", "DFlash"], "token-level CE/KL training does not maximise accepted length": ["LK losses", "GTO", "VAT"], "one fused target feature drops what later draft positions need": ["KVShot"], "trained block / TTT horizon caps length; past it acceptance collapses": ["Attention Drift"], "fixed tree budget ignores round difficulty, hardware and load": ["ECHO"], "RL rollouts: long tail dominates, static drafters go stale": ["ReSpec", "TLT"]}, "catalogue": {"contribution": "Drops feature regression for direct token prediction from fused low/mid/high target features, trained with 'training-time test' that feeds the drafter its own multi-step predictions. Acceptance then keeps improving with more drafter training data.", "limitation": "No limitations section; caveats: gains shrink with batch (SGLang 1.38x at bs 64, vLLM ~1.01x at bs 56) and 405B/671B targets untested. Serving runs used chains of only 2-3 tokens."}}

