{"key": "ddtree", "name": "DDTree", "date": "2026-04", "arxiv": "2604.12989", "skill": "best-first tree over marginals", "solves": [["DFlash", "verifies one draft path; other per- position candidates thrown away"]], "later_fixes": {"marginal-scored trees mis-rank paths; children ignore their parent": ["JetSpec", "PCTree", "DominoTree", "DARTree", "TreeSpark", "TreeFlash", "Weaver", "TAPS", "GRAFT", "PRESTO"], "fixed tree budget ignores round difficulty, hardware and load": ["TreeSpark", "GRAFT", "CAST", "BASTION", "CaDDTree"]}, "catalogue": {"contribution": "Builds a draft tree from one DFlash pass by taking the B highest-probability prefixes under the factorized per-position marginals (provably optimal for that surrogate), found with a best-first heap. The tree is verified in one target pass with an ancestor-only mask by walking the target's own greedy/sampled token.", "limitation": "Scope (no limitations section): single-stream HF Transformers harness at batch 1 with SDPA tree attention on Qwen3-4B/8B/Coder-30B-A3B. Node scores are unconditioned marginals, and the budget is picked per cell from 16-1024 (speedup peaks at 256-512 on H200)."}}

{"key": "domino", "name": "Domino", "date": "2026-05", "arxiv": "2605.29707", "skill": "GRU causal logit correction", "solves": [["DFlash", "positions drafted independently: suffix acceptance decays"]], "later_fixes": {"verifies one draft path; other per- position candidates thrown away": ["DominoTree", "DARTree"]}, "catalogue": {"contribution": "Adds to a DFlash backbone a 'Domino head': a GRU (d=1024) over embeddings of previously sampled draft tokens plus a low-rank (r=256) logit-space residual correction, run as a fused cheap sequential loop. Trained teacher-forced with a base-anchored curriculum that anneals loss weight from backbone logits to corrected logits to prevent backbone collapse.", "limitation": "Paper-stated: targets inference rather than training cost, implementation mainly adapted to SGLang, and speedup varies across hardware. Scope: Qwen3-4B/8B only, concurrency \u226432, and headline tables compare against public DFlash checkpoints trained on different data."}}

{"key": "dflare", "name": "DFlare", "date": "2026-06", "arxiv": "2606.02091", "skill": "layer-wise target fusion, scaling", "solves": [["DFlash", "one fused target feature drops what later draft positions need"]], "later_fixes": {"trained block / TTT horizon caps length; past it acceptance collapses": ["DBloom"]}, "catalogue": {"contribution": "Replaces DFlash's single fused target feature with per-draft-layer softmax mixtures over 9 target layers (separate K/V projections for target context), so deeper drafters keep improving; scales training data from 800K to 2.4M samples.", "limitation": "Stated: high training cost (32 GPUs, ~100-160 h per drafter) and data beyond 2.4M unexplored. Depth tested only to 7 layers; extra depth barely moves speedup."}}

{"key": "dspark", "name": "DSpark", "date": "2026-07", "arxiv": "2607.05147", "skill": "Markov correction head; confidence- scheduled verify length", "solves": [["DFlash", "positions drafted independently: suffix acceptance decays"], ["DFlash", "large batches: verification turns compute-bound, speedup vanishes"]], "later_fixes": {"positions drafted independently: suffix acceptance decays": ["xPress", "Parallel Blindness"], "verifies one draft path; other per- position candidates thrown away": ["PCTree", "TreeSpark"], "target work on rejected positions is thrown away": ["Carryover"], "token-level CE/KL training does not maximise accepted length": ["EDR"]}, "catalogue": {"contribution": "Semi-AR drafter: DFlash parallel backbone plus a cheap sequential head (low-rank r=256 Markov transition bias from the previous sampled token, or a GRU-style RNN head) adding prefix-dependent logit bias while keeping exact per-token softmax probabilities. A calibrated confidence head (trained on 1-TV, sequential temperature scaling) drives a hardware-aware scheduler that picks per-request verification length to maximize expected accepted tokens x engine steps/s, with early stopping to stay lossless.", "limitation": "Paper-stated: the full \u03b3-block draft cost is still paid upfront and is unrecoverable for low-acceptance queries. Scope: offline acceptance measured chain-only at T=1 on Qwen3/Gemma4 \u226414B; production uses \u03b3=5 with an asynchronous scheduler whose losslessness argument r

